  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given, the electromagnetic wave is propagating in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e.,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;direction.</p><p>The relation between the magnitudes of electric field, magnetic field and the speed of light is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>C</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>We know that the direction of propagation of electromagnetic wave is along&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
